ommand to run cellular satelleite info.py

Got it. To make this work seamlessly inside Docker, I have gone ahead and updated the paths in cellular_satelliite_info.py to look for the files at /app/create_runtime_files/ (which is the path inside the container).

Since the container doesn't automatically have access to your host machine's /home/dell/... folders, we first need to copy the files into it.

Please run these two commands in your terminal (you can do this outside the virtual environment, just a normal terminal):

1. Copy your test files from your host machine into the backend Docker container:

bash
docker cp /home/dell/Documents/July_21/create_runtime_files himshravan-backend:/app/
2. Run the script inside the Docker container:

bash
docker exec -it himshravan-backend python scripts/cognent/cellular_satelliite_info.py
This will launch the dashboard right there in your terminal, using the Docker environment which already has pandas and django fully installed!


